    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: linux/dim: Fix divide by 0 in RDMA DIM (CVE-2022-49670)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: 6fire: fix use-after-free on disconnect (CVE-2026-31581)\n\n* kernel: sctp: purge outqueue on stale COOKIE-ECHO handling (CVE-2026-52924)\n\n* kernel: net: pull headers in qdisc_pkt_len_segs_init() (CVE-2026-53091)\n\n* kernel: dm log: fix out-of-bounds write due to region_count overflow (CVE-2026-53059)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: conntrack: remove sprintf usage (CVE-2026-53002)\n\n* kernel: tipc: fix double-free in tipc_buf_append() (CVE-2026-52993)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: l2cap: Add missing chan lock in l2cap_ecred_reconf_rsp (CVE-2026-53071)\n\n* kernel: zram: fix use-after-free in zram_bvec_write_partial() (CVE-2026-53185)\n\n* kernel: i2c: stub: Reject I2C block transfers with invalid length (CVE-2026-64191)\n\n* kernel: AMD-SN-7061: Safe RET Interrupt Vulnerability (CVE-2026-68480)\n\n* kernel: net: qrtr: restrict socket creation to the initial network namespace (CVE-2026-68294)\n\n* kernel: dm-verity: fix buffer overflow in FEC calculation (CVE-2026-72098)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: flowtable: publish GC-visible tuple last (CVE-2026-74746)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Backport 9aca491e0dcc (\"Set fc_nlinfo in nh_create_ipv4, nh_create_ipv6\") [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-155585)\n\n* GNR-D: kdump and manual kexec result in hard system freeze with no console output [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-168729)\n\n* RHEL9.4 - dasd: Fix PPRC copy pair swap state and format information. [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-176467)\n\n* RT scheduler livelock: migrate-disabled task at pushable-list head causes repeated RT push/stopper retries, starving a critical RT task (remaining issue after CVE-2026-45919 fix in 94894c9c477e) [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-257979)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
